%description:
Tests an explicit read after a received FIN. The server application reads
only by READ commands (autoRead=false). The client sends 500 bytes and then
closes. The READ at t=1.2 takes 300 bytes. The FIN arrives at t=1.502 and
advances rcv_nxt to 502, but a FIN puts no byte into the receive queue. The
READ at t=2 asks for 300 bytes, and it must stop at the FIN: the application
gets the last 200 bytes. Before the repair, the read asked the queue for one
sequence number more than it held, and the simulation stopped at an
assertion.
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true

*.tcptester.cmdenv-log-level=DEBUG
*.srv_app.cmdenv-log-level=INFO
**.cmdenv-log-level=OFF

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 500"
*.cli_app.tClose=1.5s
*.srv_app.autoRead=false
*.srv_app.readScript="1.2 300; 2.0 300"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%contains: stdout
[1.501 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A F ack 501 win 16384

%# the READ after the FIN gets the rest of the data
%contains: stdout
TcpTestNet1.srv_app: received 500 bytes in 2 packets

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
